/Title (God tells Avram to leave his home and travel to a new land called Canaan. Avram trusts G-od and follows His words. When there is no food because of hunger, Avram and his wife Sarai go to Egypt. Later, they return to Canaan Avram and his nephew Lot decide to live in different places. When Lot is taken prisoner, Avraam bravely fights .to save him G-od promises Avram that his children and grandchildren will have the land of Canaan. Avram and Sarai do not have children, but Go-d promises that Abram will have a big family. Later, Go-d changes their names to Avraham and Sarah. Avraham continues to . believe in Go-d and follow His commands Avraham teaches us to have faith in G-od, even when life is difficult. We can trust God, keep doing what is right, and stay hopeful when things do not happen as we expect .)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 147 0 R
